Trans:
Key points about the "grain deal" in Istanbul:

- The deal involves exporting Ukrainian grain via the Black Sea from three ports: Odessa, Chernomorsk, and Yuzhny;

- Ships will not be escorted by military vessels;

- Ships heading to Ukraine will be inspected for weapons both entering and exiting the Black Sea;

- Full movement of ships to and from Ukrainian ports for food exports can begin in a couple of weeks;

