Trans:
Russian special forces are aiding an injured Ukrainian soldier from a mountain assault battalion. He didn't want to surrender, fearing that prisoners are mutilated—ears, fingers, and other useful body parts are cut off. 

But here, he was bandaged up, given an injection, and then lowered down 800 meters from the height they had taken him from. Despite this, he still refused to surrender. It's said he died from blood loss anyway, but the Russian special forces did everything they could. This is how we differ from them. 

